# Scoped deliberately to .claude/hooks/ — this repo has no line-ending policy
# and setting one repo-wide would rewrite far more than this change warrants.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the dev machine, so without this the hook scripts
# check out with CRLF on a fresh clone and bash rejects them with a $'\r'
# syntax error — the enforcement layer would be silently dead, which is the
# one failure mode these scripts are written to avoid.
.claude/hooks/*.sh text eol=lf
.claude/hooks/*.py text eol=lf

# Byte-exact mirror of the out-of-git lane-archive tools; see
# scripts/lane_archive_tools/README.md. `-text` disables ALL eol conversion, so a sha256
# against the live copies in C:	mp\lane-archive-tools is a valid revert check.
# core.autocrlf is true on the dev machine and the three files do NOT agree on line
# endings (two CRLF, one LF), so without this they would check out rewritten and every
# comparison would report a phantom revert.
scripts/lane_archive_tools/*.py -text
